NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.A has 16 observations and 2 variables.

5953       ;
5954       proc hpnlmod data=a out=b;
5955       parms alpha=.45 beta=.05 gamma=-.0025;
5956       x0 = -.5*beta / gamma;
5957       if (x < x0) then
5958       yp = alpha + beta*x + gamma *x*x;
5959       else
5960       yp = alpha + beta*x0 + gamma*x0*x0;
5961       model y ~ residual(yp);
5962       estimate 'join point' -beta/2/gamma;
5963       estimate 'plateau value c' alpha - beta**2/(4*gamma);
5964       predict 'predicted' yp pred=yp;
5965       predict 'response' y pred=y;
5966       predict 'x' x pred=x;
5967       run;


NOTE: The HPNLMOD procedure is executing in single-machine mode.
